Render-only test of the mail mode (KMail's message viewer)

A message shown by the part in mail mode may only be laid out and painted:
nothing it contains may make the part (or WebKit) look up a name or open a
connection.  Each file in messages/ is one family of tricks (DNS
prefetching, preconnect, prefetch/preload/prerender/modulepreload,
speculation rules, <a ping> with a real click, srcset/imagesrcset, CSS
url()/@import/image-set()/@font-face, meta refresh, <base>, forms, frames,
object/embed/applet/portal, remote style sheets and fonts, favicons and
manifests, scripts of every kind, media, others); 00-control.html is plain
HTML that must render.  Every message carries a red box: the driver counts
red pixels of a screenshot (layout and paint happened).

  kwpe-render-only [--external] [--wait MS] MESSAGE.html
      the driver (built with the part, not installed): the part from
      KWPE_PART (library name or path) with "mode=mail", as KMail creates
      it; MESSAGE.html as an HTML part in a frame of a host document, in a
      private directory.  Prints COMPLETED, LINK <url> (a click handed to
      the host), RENDERED <red pixels>.
  kwpe-sanitize [html|css] [content|host] [render-only|external]
      the first layer alone: what WebKit gets of a document (stdin).
  run.sh BUILD_DIR [OUT_DIR]
      everything in a podman container with its own network namespace:
      inner.sh gives it 10.77.0.1 with a logging DNS server (dnslog.py,
      the only resolver; it answers every name with 10.77.0.1) and a
      logging HTTP server (httplog.py), a default route (every connection
      attempt sends a packet), nftables counters of DNS queries, TCP SYNs
      and other UDP packets, tcpdump on every interface.  Every message
      runs in a fresh driver process and HOME in these configurations:
        all            every layer: 0 DNS queries, 0 connection attempts,
                       0 packets at all (not even to the closed proxy)
        no-<layer>     one layer switched off (KWPE_MAIL_TEST_DISABLE_LAYERS:
                       sanitizer, settings, csp, filter, proxy): still 0
                       DNS queries, 0 connections other than to the part's
                       closed proxy on 127.0.0.1, 0 HTTP requests
        no-layers      every layer off: the measurement must see lookups
                       and connections (it is not blind)
        external       "load external references": only image, style and
                       font requests (Sec-Fetch-Dest), only lookups of
                       hosts they went to; external-allowed.html must load
                       all three kinds
      It exits 0 only if every run passed; summary.txt names each run
      (FAIL lines say why), every run's directory keeps the driver's
      output, the DNS and HTTP logs and the pcap.
      Parameters (environment): IMAGE (default localhost/kwpe-render-only,
      see Containerfile), KDE3_PREFIX, QT3_PREFIX (mounted read-only,
      default /opt/kde3, /opt/kde3-qt), WAIT (ms per message, default
      5000), CONFIGS, MESSAGES (paths inside the container: /test/messages/..).

On t590 (through the harness, reserved: ice-harness -H t590 reserve
--reason "..." --max 90m; release afterwards), in a work directory there
with the source tree in src/ and the WebKit RPMs in ctx/rpms/:

  podman build -t localhost/kwpe-render-only -f src/tests/render-only/Containerfile ctx
  podman run --rm --network=none --security-opt label=disable -v $PWD:/work -v /opt/kde3:/opt/kde3:ro \
      -v /opt/kde3-qt:/opt/kde3-qt:ro localhost/kwpe-render-only sh -c \
      'cmake -G Ninja -S /work/src -B /work/build -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/kde3 && ninja -C /work/build'
  src/tests/render-only/run.sh build out; echo $?

Nothing is installed: the part is the one in the build directory.  The
container needs CAP_NET_ADMIN and CAP_NET_RAW in its own (rootless)
network namespace for nftables and tcpdump; nothing reaches the host's
network (--network=none).
